" Title: Meridian Marine Ltd Remote and Flexible Working Policy\n\n1. **Policy Statement**\n   Meridian Marine Ltd recognizes the benefits of remote and flexible working arrangements for both employees and the company. This policy outlines the conditions under which eligible staff may work remotely or on a flexible schedule.\n\n2. **Eligibility and Service Requirement**\n   Employees who have successfully completed a probationary period of 6 months are eligible to apply for remote or flexible working arrangements, subject to departmental approval.\n\n3. **Remote Work Allowance**\n   Eligible employees may work remotely up to three (3) days per week. The decision regarding the number of remote days will be made on a case-by-case basis, considering the employee's role, responsibilities, and performance.\n\n4. **Core Working Hours**\n   Core working hours for all employees will remain 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM local time (Monday to Friday). Employees are expected to maintain these hours when working remotely, with flexibility allowed within reason to accommodate different time zones or personal circumstances.\n\n5. **Home Office Equipment Allowance**\n   Upon approval of a remote work arrangement, employees will receive an allowance of $1,000 USD for home office equipment setup. This one-time allowance can be claimed after the first month of remote work. Additional equipment needs beyond this initial allowance should be discussed with management on a case-by-case basis.\n\n6. **Equipment Maintenance and Replacement**\n   Employees are responsible for maintaining their home office equipment in good working condition. Meridian Marine Ltd will consider requests for replacement or upgrade of equipment every 2 years, based on operational needs and justification provided by the employee.\n\n7. **Working Abroad**\n   Employees may work temporarily from abroad for up to 30 consecutive days per year. This requires prior approval from management and must not disrupt the employee's ability to perform their duties effectively or compromise company confidentiality.\n\n8. **Approval Process**\n   Employees interested in a remote or flexible working arrangement should submit a written request to their department head, outlining their proposed schedule, reasons for the request, and any anticipated challenges. Approval will be based on the employee's job role, performance, and the potential impact on the department and company.\n\n9. **Review and Revision**\n   This policy will be reviewed annually to ensure it remains aligned with business needs and employee requirements. Suggestions for policy improvements are welcome and should be submitted in writing to the HR department.\n\n10. **Policy Compliance**\n   Employees who violate this policy may have their remote or flexible working privileges revoked at management's discretion. Any questions or concerns regarding this policy should be directed to the HR department."